        <text><![CDATA[Continuous compounding uses the constant e.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A = P(1 + r/n)⁽ⁿᵗ⁾]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is compound interest n times per year.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A = P + I]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is a total amount relationship, not continuous compounding.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q17</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q17</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>A loan has $90 simple interest after 3 years at 5%. What was the principal?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$600]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[90 = P(0.05)(3), so P = 600.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$30]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This divides interest by time only.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$150]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This uses 0.05 incorrectly.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$1,800]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This multiplies by time and rate instead of dividing.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q18</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q18</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.2</p><p>For A = 700(1.02)ᵗ, what is the annual growth rate?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[2]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This would mean 200%, not 2%.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[2%]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The growth factor 1.02 corresponds to a 2% rate.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[20%]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A 20% growth factor would be 1.20.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[102%]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[1.02 is the factor, not the rate.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q19</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q19</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>Which situation is modeled by simple interest?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Interest added to the balance and then earning more interest]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That is compound interest.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Money doubled every year]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That is exponential growth.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The same dollar amount of interest added each year]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Simple interest adds a constant amount.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Interest compounded daily]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That is compound interest.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q20</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q20</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.2</p><p>Which account grows fastest if principal, rate, and time are the same?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Simple interest]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Simple interest does not earn interest on interest.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Annual compounding]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Annual compounding grows, but less often than monthly or continuous.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Continuous compounding]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Continuous compounding gives the greatest amount for the same positive rate and time.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Monthly compounding]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Monthly is frequent, but continuous compounding is the limiting case.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q21</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q21</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>A savings account starts with 200 dollars and increases by 25 dollars each month. Which expression gives the balance after m months?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200m + 25]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This treats the starting amount as repeated each month.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[25 + m + 200]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This adds months instead of multiplying by the monthly amount.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200 + 25m]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The starting amount is 200 and each month adds 25 dollars.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200 - 25m]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This models a decrease, not an increase.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q22</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q22</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>If an item costs 80 dollars and is discounted by 25 percent, what is the discount amount?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[25 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This uses the percent number as dollars without calculating the percent of 80.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[55 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is the sale price, not the discount amount.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[105 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This adds the percent number to the original price.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[20 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[25 percent of 80 is 20.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q23</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q23</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>An item costs 80 dollars and is discounted by 25 percent. What is the sale price?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[60 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The discount is 20 dollars, so 80 - 20 = 60.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[20 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is the discount amount, not the final price.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[100 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This adds the discount instead of subtracting it.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[55 dollars]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This subtracts 25 dollars instead of 25 percent of 80.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q24</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q24</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>Why is it important to identify the starting amount in a financial model?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It is always the same as the monthly change]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The starting amount and rate can be different.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It anchors the model before repeated change is applied]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The starting amount is the initial value in the situation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It should be ignored after the first step]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The starting amount remains part of the model.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It makes every model quadratic]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Financial models can be linear, exponential, or another type.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG1_U06_L06_Q25</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG1_U06_L06_Q25</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A1.DF.1</p><p>What does a percent increase do to an original amount?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Adds a percent of the original amount to the original]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A percent increase raises the original by a calculated percent.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Always subtracts from the original]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That describes a decrease or discount.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Divides the original by the percent number only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That is not how percent increase is calculated.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Leaves the original unchanged]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[An increase changes the amount.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>